id: liquid-form
name: Liquid Form
type: instant
actionCost: 0
kiCost: 0
attacking: false
requiresTarget: false
special: true
usageLimit: 1/round
togglesState: liquid
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Liquefy, or solidify again. One Maneuver both ways: it puts you into the Liquid
  Special State, and used again it takes you out.
text: >
  Liquid Form Maneuver [1/Round]: You are able to liquefy your body, allowing you to
  become amorphous, move as you please, and fit into smaller spaces.
  –Maneuver Type: Instant Maneuver
  –Action Cost: N/A
  –Minions: N/A
  –KP Cost: N/A
  –Effect: You enter the Liquid Special State. If you use this Maneuver while in the
  Liquid Special State, you exit the Liquid Special State.

---

# The whole of the Maneuver is a switch, and `togglesState` is what says which State it
# throws. Which way it goes is read when it is used rather than written in the file: "if
# you use this Maneuver while in the Liquid Special State, you exit" is one Maneuver with
# two outcomes, not two Maneuvers.
#
# Done in code rather than as a script because a script cannot ask what happened first: a
# block that left the State and then asked whether it was still in it would be reading a
# change that has not landed. What the State is worth is in the State's own file, which is
# where a reader looks for it.
#
# An Instant, so the Instant rule comes with it: not two in a row, and only in answer to a
# Standard Maneuver. Turning back solid is as much an Instant as turning liquid, which the
# entry settles by making them the same Maneuver.
#
# --- What is not built ----------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The Liquid State's sixth effect. Said in that file, with why.
#
# "Move as you please, and fit into smaller spaces" is the tagline rather than the Effect,
# and what it buys is the Size Category the State takes off you.
#
# --- How it is gained ------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# A Special Maneuver, and what opens it has not been read yet.
